From e6396f89e9c2704e5a1866f041040c1160bb71f3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 14:00:34 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] slimbus: ngd: return transaction allocation errors before
 power requests

Carry this reviewed SLIMbus/BAM change into maintained Linux 6.18.
Preserve the existing LTS channel-removal/reconfigure protocol, socket
interfaces and DMA provider implementation. This stage is exact patch.

The completed eighteen-change series passes 3,221 source-bound synthetic
cases and 117 independent regression controls, with normal LeakSanitizer
and fail-fast address/undefined-behavior sanitizers. These cover
startup, child and parent ownership, QMI allocation, TX completion
lifetime, synchronous/asynchronous response ownership, DMA admission and
the retained LTS stream caller. Baselines from the appropriate
intermediate stages fail their targeted assertions. All 108 ARM, ARM64
and ARM64 RT component objects build with W=1 and nonpermissive CFI
without diagnostics; their ELF source checksums match the final
candidate.

Kernel waits, workqueues, IDR, PM, packets, DMA and device services in
the host models are synthetic. No real firmware, audio, hardware,
network, phone or installed package executes. Full current-kernel link,
physical DMA-stop/recovery and final-image acceptance remain
unqualified. Codex prepared the LTS adaptations and qualification.
Preserve original authors, dates, notices and assistance credits. Human
DCO and owner, security and subsystem review remain pending; no new
sign-off is added.

Original reviewed changelog and provenance:

qmi_txn_init() returns a negative errno if IDR allocation fails. The
power-request helper overwrites that result and sends an unregistered
transaction, then waits for or cancels its truncated transaction ID.
This can also remove an unrelated transaction with that ID.

Return the allocation error before sending, waiting or cancelling.
Accept both zero and positive transaction IDs, matching the existing
select-instance helper.

Codex generated the fix and a host model using six exact NGD/QMI
callback bodies with logical IDR, completion and socket services. The
model passes 576 cases and 7,008 checks after 896 baseline failures;
five regression controls are rejected. Eight ARM/ARM64 objects build
with LLVM21 W=1 and strict callback checks without diagnostics. No real
QMI, DMA, audio, phone or network operations execute. Hardware stop
ordering and failed-suspend rollback remain open. Human review and DCO
certification remain pending.

Fixes: 917809e2280b ("slimbus: ngd: Add qcom SLIMBus NGD driver")

Backported from commit ed2c35d1391f ("slimbus: ngd: return transaction
allocation errors before power requests")
---
 drivers/slimbus/qcom-ngd-ctrl.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/slimbus/qcom-ngd-ctrl.c b/drivers/slimbus/qcom-ngd-ctrl.c
index ba9ac5531ef49..a0af6a80982cc 100644
--- a/drivers/slimbus/qcom-ngd-ctrl.c
+++ b/drivers/slimbus/qcom-ngd-ctrl.c
@@ -422,6 +422,8 @@ static int qcom_slim_qmi_send_power_request(struct qcom_slim_ngd_ctrl *ctrl,
 
 	rc = qmi_txn_init(ctrl->qmi.handle, &txn,
 				slimbus_power_resp_msg_v01_ei, &resp);
+	if (rc < 0)
+		return rc;
 
 	rc = qmi_send_request(ctrl->qmi.handle, NULL, &txn,
 				SLIMBUS_QMI_POWER_REQ_V01,
-- 
2.56.0

